### Step 2: Multi-Stage Builds

Multi-stage builds in Docker can help reduce the size of your final image by separating the build process into distinct stages. This can further optimize your pipeline by reducing the amount of data that needs to be transferred and stored.

### Step 3: Parallel Builds

Leverage Jenkins' ability to run parallel builds to speed up your pipeline. This can be particularly effective when combined with Docker, as each build can run in its own isolated container.

