### 2. Enable Keepalive Connections
Keepalive connections can reduce the overhead of establishing new connections.

### 3. Use HTTP/2 or HTTP/3
HTTP/2 and HTTP/3 can improve performance by enabling multiplexing and reducing latency.

### 4. Adjust Buffer Sizes
Optimize buffer sizes to handle larger requests and responses more efficiently.

### 5. Use Cache
Cache frequently accessed content to reduce the load on backend servers.

### 6. Enable Gzip Compression
Compress responses to reduce the amount of data transferred over the network.

### 7. Use Connection Pooling
Pool connections to backend servers to reduce the overhead of establishing new connections.

### 8. Tune Worker Processes
