Schedule regular security scans to ensure that your dependencies are continuously checked for vulnerabilities. You can use the scheduling features of your CI/CD tool to run the pipeline at regular intervals (e.g., daily, weekly).

### Step 7: Monitor and Audit
Set up monitoring and auditing to track the effectiveness of your automated security patch management system. Use tools like Splunk, ELK Stack, or built-in logging features of your CI/CD tool to monitor the pipeline's performance and security posture.

### Step 8: Educate and Train
Educate your development team on the importance of security and the new automated patch management system. Provide training sessions and documentation to ensure everyone understands how to use the system effectively.

